## 3. Key Decisions & Conventions
- Card data: Use Godot Resources (.tres) for each card (name, art, cost, ATK, DEF, effect script); load dynamically from CardDatabase.gd
- Turns: Player goes first then resolve, enemy goes then resolve
- Mana: Resets to 3 at the start of each player's turn, unless modified by an item or card that round
- Naming: PascalCase for classes (CardDatabase), snake_case for variables/functions (draw_card)
- Signals: Use autoload Signals.gd for global events (card_played, turn_ended, battle_won)
- Adult Content: Mature themes via Dialogic; keep separate from core mechanics
- Save System: JSON files for decks/progress/inventory/story choices/faction standings; auto-save after battles
- Waifu Selection: Max 3 active companions; buffs only apply if conditions met (e.g. affection >5)
- Story Choices: Branching paths from player decisions; factions affected by help/hinder choices; culminates in demon invasion with multiple endings (world saved but losses, bad ending where demons win)
- Mobile Support: Planned for Android/iOS but low priority due to TOS concerns; touch input, responsive UI scaling, performance optimization
- UI Scaling & Positioning: No hardcoded positions or fixed pixel coordinates for UI elements. Use anchors, containers, and percent-based sizing/margins for fully responsive layout across resolutions (PC and mobile prep)
- Paths in Godot: All paths start with res:// (Godot's virtual root). Example: res://scripts/cards/Card.gd (points to project_folder/scripts/cards/Card.gd)

